<Layout title="Technology · Space Array" active="technology.html">

<main>
  <section class="hero"><div class="kicker">Technology roadmap</div><h1>From enabling technologies to an operational array.</h1><p class="lead">The Space Array initiative connects science requirements to the technologies needed for formation-flying interferometry in space.</p></section>
  <section class="grid">
    <article class="card"><h3>Relative navigation</h3><p>GNSS, inter-satellite ranging, orbit determination, and baseline reconstruction.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Time and frequency</h3><p>Clock stability, synchronization, phase transfer, and calibration architectures.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Receivers</h3><p>Millimetre and sub-millimetre receiver technologies suitable for space operation.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Data transport</h3><p>Optical links, onboard storage, compression, and downlink strategies.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Correlation</h3><p>On-ground and distributed correlation architectures for long-baseline observations.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Imaging</h3><p>Calibration, sparse arrays, dynamic imaging, and high-fidelity reconstruction.</p></article>
  </section>
</main>

